.TH SMART-MODE 1 "2026" "SmartMode" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
smart-mode \- switch light and dark mode from the sun and room brightness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smart-mode
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smart-mode
puts an icon in the system tray and switches the desktop between light and dark mode.
It uses the sun's position at a configured location, cloud cover from Open-Meteo,
and the ambient light sensor when the machine has one.
On Cinnamon it switches the Mint-Y themes; elsewhere it sets the GNOME color scheme with
.BR gsettings (1).
.PP
Set a location from the tray menu. Settings live in
.IR ~/.config/smart-mode/config.yaml .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/smart-mode/config.yaml
Settings, reloaded when saved.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/smart-mode.desktop
Created by the "Launch at login" menu toggle.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/hopskipnfall/SmartMode
